hey guys my name is David Thomas and I'm  the founder of wire watches today I'm  going to show you how to set up the  midnight collection timepiece in this  video I'll teach you how to connect the  strap to the watch how to adjust the  date and the time and also how to make  sure the mesh and metal strap fits your  wrist perfectly so let's get started  all midnight collection timepieces come  with a quick-release band to remove  simply pull the lever on the back side  to replace it with the same or a  different strap the process is the same  as the original collection align the pin  at the top with the hole at the top of  the watch pull the pin and slide in  until you hear a click once you hear it  click make sure it's secure and you're  good to go to change the date push the  crown in all the way and unclick at once  spin the crown and the date should  change accordingly when you're ready  pull the crown out once more and you  should be able to adjust the time to  your current location after you finished  push the crown back in all the way and  your watch is set to adjust the length  of the mesh strap open the butterfly  clip take the tools supplied with the  watch and insert it into the hole  leverage it backwards and up at the same  time and it should click open slide the  clip to your current resize and close it  by pushing firmly back down  to remove links from a metal strap take  note of the directional arrows on the  back insert the tool supplied with the  watch in the holes tap lightly until the  pin appears on the other side once it  does remove the pin completely and the  link should fall out take as many links  out as you need and once you're happy  place the pin back in to connect the  final links tap lightly with a hammer  and secure it to the watch when you're  ready
 

